\*
\* 0-RTT ticket single-use, fail-closed guard, and reconnect replay.
\*
\* Safety claims (states and steps that must be unreachable):
\*   EarlyDataRequiresFreshAccept: early data is accepted only once, after a good binder, with the guard free
\*   FailClosedDoesNotBurnOrAccept: a busy or checked-out replay guard accepts nothing and does not burn the ticket
\*   BadBinderDoesNotBurnOrAccept: a bad binder is rejected before the guard and does not burn the ticket
\*   AcceptsAtMostOnce: one boot accepts the ticket at most once; a crash before the deferred fsync is not this count
\*   DurableAcceptStaysBurned: once the journal fsync has landed, that accept is still burned
\*   RestartUndoesUndurableAccept: a restart before fsync clears the in-memory accept
\*   FullOrClashDoesNotBurn: CacheFull and an 8-byte nonce-prefix collision decide the ticket without burning it
\*   RelayWaitsForHandshake: relay bytes are sent only after the handshake, a verified probe, and Safari SETTINGS
\*   RetainOnlyVerified: the QUIC leg is retained only after a verified probe, Safari SETTINGS, and the handshake
\*   StoreTicketOnlyVerified: the next resumption ticket is stored only after a verified probe and Safari SETTINGS
\*   SettingsFailDoesNotStore: a verified probe that fails the Safari SETTINGS check does not retain or store a ticket
\*   VerifiedProbeImpliesHandshake: a verified probe implies the handshake completed
\*   ReplayDoesNotAcceptAgain: a second offer of an accepted ticket is rejected and does not increment accepts
\*   DeadDropsTheAttempt: a handshake timeout installs no relay, retain, or stored ticket
\*   DecidedImpliesOffered: the server decides a ticket only after the client has consumed it
\*   HandshakeFollowsEarlyProbe: on this 0-RTT path the handshake follows an early probe

